-- title:
--   Quadratic algebras with unit discriminant over reduced rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is reduced, i.e. whose only nilpotent element is $0$, and let $t, n \in R$ be elements such that $t^2 - 4n$ is a unit of $R$. Then the quotient ring $R[X]/(X^2 - tX + n)$, formed as the `AdjoinRoot` construction applied to the polynomial $X^2 - C(t) \cdot X + C(n) \in R[X]$, is again reduced: every nilpotent element of this quadratic $R$-algebra is zero. No further hypotheses are imposed on $R$; in particular $R$ is not assumed Noetherian, local or nontrivial, and the statement is not an assertion about the quadratic extension being étale or separable, only about the absence of nonzero nilpotents.
--
--   This is the monogenic quadratic case of the fact that an étale algebra over a reduced ring is reduced, the unit discriminant $t^2-4n$ being exactly the condition that $X^2-tX+n$ be separable over each residue field of $R$. It is used in the project to see that the residue algebra of the commutative order generated by an integral element of $GL_2$ with unit discriminant is reduced, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.LevelP.TorsionPointRing.isReduced_of_isUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelP.TorsionPointRing.isReduced_of_isUnit) and by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_normString_eq_toTensorGL_of_mem_localIntegralSet_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one_of_prime`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_normString_eq_toTensorGL_of_mem_localIntegralSet_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one_of_prime).
